From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: a child window destroyed with the focus inside it gives the focus to its parent

DestroyWindow takes the keyboard focus away from the window it destroys;
for a visible child window that has the focus itself, the focus goes to
its parent (Wine's own message tests record that sequence on Windows).
Wine did that only through hiding the window, so a child window
destroyed while one of its own children had the focus, or while it was
already hidden, took the focus down with it: the focus was left on
nothing, and the keys went to no window of the program.

AnyDesk's "Connecting..." panel is such a window: AnyDesk puts the focus
on its Cancel button, and once connected hides the panel's backdrop and
destroys the panel with it. On Windows the keys typed then go to the
remote computer; here they went nowhere until the AnyDesk window was
clicked away from and back (David, 2026-10-05). The window being
destroyed now gives the focus to its parent when it, or a window inside
it, has it.

Wine's user32 win and msg tests give the same results with and without
the change (win: no failures; msg: the same failures).

Test: test/destroyfocus-gate.sh with test/destroyfocus-probe.c (mutant
SG_MUTANT_DESTROY_FOCUS).
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/window.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/window.c
@@ -5389,6 +5389,14 @@
     return 0;
 }
 
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DESTROY_FOCUS
+/* whether the focus window is a descendant of a window */
+static BOOL focus_is_inside( HWND hwnd, HWND focus )
+{
+    return is_child( hwnd, focus );
+}
+#endif
+
 /***********************************************************************
  *           NtUserDestroyWindow (win32u.@)
  */
@@ -5434,6 +5442,25 @@
                                 SWP_NOZORDER | SWP_NOACTIVATE | SWP_HIDEWINDOW );
     }
 
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_DESTROY_FOCUS
+    /* a child window being destroyed gives up the focus to its parent when
+     * it or a window inside it has it (hiding it above does that only when
+     * it is visible and has the focus itself); else the focus is left on
+     * nothing and the keys go nowhere -- AnyDesk's "Connecting" panel held
+     * the focus on its Cancel button and hid its backdrop before the
+     * backdrop was destroyed */
+    if (is_child && is_window( hwnd ))
+    {
+        HWND focus = get_focus();
+        if (focus && (focus == hwnd || focus_is_inside( hwnd, focus )))
+        {
+            HWND parent = NtUserGetAncestor( hwnd, GA_PARENT );
+            if (parent == get_desktop_window()) parent = 0;
+            NtUserSetFocus( parent );
+        }
+    }
+#endif
+
     if (!is_window( hwnd )) return TRUE;
 
     /* Recursively destroy child windows */
